.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-generate 1  "generate " 
.SH NAME
murk\-generate \- Generate a random secret and store it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk generate\fR [\fB\-\-length\fR] [\fB\-\-hex\fR] [\fB\-\-desc\fR] [\fB\-\-example\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a random secret and store it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-length\fR \fI<LENGTH>\fR [default: 32]
Length in bytes
.TP
\fB\-\-hex\fR
Encode the value as hex instead of URL\-safe base64
.TP
\fB\-\-desc\fR \fI<DESC>\fR
Description of the secret
.TP
\fB\-\-example\fR \fI<EXAMPLE>\fR
Example value
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
Who can read the secret: `everyone`, `me` (a private value for you only) or a group name (experimental). Omit it to keep an existing secret\*(Aqs tier. A new secret is shared with everyone
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Tag for grouping (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Name of the secret
